cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Manifesto: protocols for digital existence — with a measured reflexive verification bound"
abstract: >-
  An open ontology for digital entities (experience, responsibility,
  identity) that grew a measured research line: the reflexive verification
  bound (health condition λ_G < (1−μ)λ_V; phase transition at μ = 1;
  delegation-invariant anchor), the coefficient μ measured for LLM
  verifiers (≈2–3 on informal claims at every depth probed, ≈0.14 on
  well-founded controls, 0 for claims compiled to deterministic checks), a
  settlement gate that catches and repairs generator hallucinations with
  priced receipts, an evidence pack sealing the episode as re-executable
  decision records, and the addressing-is-equality idiom with its measured
  five-orders cost asymmetry. Papers in papers/ carry claims checkers that
  recount their figures from the repository.
message: "If you use or evaluate this work, please cite it."
